{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01HT97cpDdd1rvoTWeWprv1B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have enough context. Now let me create the planning artifacts. The plan is:\n\n## Planning Documents to Create\n\n1. `docs/01_requirements/QuantAgent-4w4-RQ-lookback-windows.md` — requirements document\n2. `docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-4w4-AC-lookback-windows.md` — acceptance criteria\n3. `docs/06_implementation/QuantAgent-4w4-IM-lookback-windows.md` — implementation notes (spec for the implementer)\n4. Update `docs/01_requirements/README.md` to add the new RQ link\n\n\n5. Update `docs/06_implementation/README.md` to add the new IM link\n6. Envelope artifacts: `result.json`, `run-report.md`, `quality-gates.log`\n\nFor the design, I'm going with the minimal approach: adding a `required_history_bars` property to `TradingStrategy` with a default of 30, which `FiftyTwoWeekHighStrategy` can override to 303. The backtest engine will use this value to compute the correct `data_start` date.\n\nI need to implement a conversion function that translates trading bars into calendar days based on the timeframe—for daily bars it's roughly `ceil(bars * 365 / 252)` to account for weekends and holidays, hourly uses a different ratio based on 6.5 trading hours per day, and 4-hour bars scale accordingly. There's a safe fallback of `bars * 2` for unknown timeframes. Existing strategies keep the current behavior with the 30-bar default for backward compatibility.\n\nThe implementation requires updating the base strategy class to expose a `required_history_bars` property, modifying the backtest module to use this property instead of the hardcoded value and adding the conversion helper, and overriding the property in the fifty-two-week high strategy to 303 bars. I'll also need to add tests to verify the lookback window calculation works correctly.\n\nFor the b8r branch interaction, the main branch implementer won't touch the fifty-two-week high strategy since it lives in the b8r branch, but the b8r team will need to add the override when merging. To test the acceptance criteria that the engine delivers over 252 bars when required, I can create a mock strategy declaring 300 bars and verify the backtest calculates the correct data start date based on trading days rather than calendar days.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the documentation — I need to be clear about what the 4w4 implementer is responsible for versus what the b8r team will handle later.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":887,"cache_read_input_tokens":63150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":887},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5f29735-d3ee-49a9-b09d-cef53776ca0b","uuid":"624ded3b-bc00-4c66-b58a-5e9a5f6ae0de"}
